{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01P1goX9y8VfzbMWXnCjn56m","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /private/tmp/h-VoLmXu/README.md has been updated successfully."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5beae75f-8665-4bbe-9db4-9327d693bbc5","uuid":"721dd432-6537-469b-bc3e-368224a56718","timestamp":"2026-11-09T19:08:41.718Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"/private/tmp/h-VoLmXu/README.md","oldString":"Lanes:\n\n- `codex`: Codex CLI (`codex exec --json`), unsandboxed.\n- `kimi`:","newString":"Lanes:\n\n- `codex`: Codex CLI (`codex exec --json`), unsandboxed.\n- `codex-sandboxed`: the same Codex run, with codex and its shell under\n  `sandbox/agent.sb` and a scratch HOME and `CODEX_HOME`. `-o` writes into a\n  scratch folder in `/tmp` and the file is copied into the run folder after\n  the sandbox exits, because the profile denies the real home (the eval\n  repository sits under it on the eval Mac). `~/.codex/auth.json` and\n  `config.toml` are copied into the scratch `CODEX_HOME` before the run.\n- `kimi`:","originalFile":"# agent-evals\n\nA small harness that runs coding agents on short tasks and keeps everything a\nrun produced, so the runs can be graded and compared later. It lives in\n`~/evals/agent-evals` on the eval Mac.\n\n`./run.sh <task> <lane> [rep]` copies `tasks/<task>/` into a scratch folder in\n`/tmp`, runs the lane's agent there with `tasks/<task>.prompt`, and writes the\nrun folder `runs/<task>-<lane>-r<rep>/`:\n\n- `prompt.txt`, `agent.log` (the agent's JSON event stream), `agent.err`,\n  `meta.json` (exit code, seconds);\n- `final.txt`, the agent's last message, for the Codex lanes;\n- `answer.json`, written by `check_answer.py`: the final answer the graders\n  read (from `final.txt` for Codex, from the event stream for Kimi).\n\nLanes:\n\n- `codex`: Codex CLI (`codex exec --json`), unsandboxed.\n- `kimi`: Kimi Code. Its output goes to Moonshot, so its shell runs under the\n  macOS sandbox profile `sandbox/agent.sb` (no reading or writing the real\n  home), with an empty scratch HOME. Kimi's own install and sessions live in\n  `~/.kimi-code`, which the profile opens.\n\nCodex logs in with an API key from the environment (`CODEX_API_KEY`), so it\nneeds nothing from the home folder.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":17,"oldLines":6,"newStart":17,"newLines":12,"lines":[" Lanes:"," "," - `codex`: Codex CLI (`codex exec --json`), unsandboxed.","+- `codex-sandboxed`: the same Codex run, with codex and its shell under","+  `sandbox/agent.sb` and a scratch HOME and `CODEX_HOME`. `-o` writes into a","+  scratch folder in `/tmp` and the file is copied into the run folder after","+  the sandbox exits, because the profile denies the real home (the eval","+  repository sits under it on the eval Mac). `~/.codex/auth.json` and","+  `config.toml` are copied into the scratch `CODEX_HOME` before the run."," - `kimi`: Kimi Code. Its output goes to Moonshot, so its shell runs under the","   macOS sandbox profile `sandbox/agent.sb` (no reading or writing the real","   home), with an empty scratch HOME. Kimi's own install and sessions live in"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false,"contentNotInModelContext":true},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01P1goX9y8VfzbMWXnCjn56m","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
