). `~/.codex/auth.json` and\n  `config.toml` are copied into the scratch `CODEX_HOME` before the run.\n- `kimi`: Kimi Code. Its output goes to Moonshot, so its shell runs under the\n  macOS sandbox profile `sandbox/agent.sb` (no reading or writing the real\n  home), with an empty scratch HOME. Kimi's own install and sessions live in\n  `~/.kimi-code`, which the profile opens.\n\nCodex logs in with an API key from the environment (`CODEX_API_KEY`), so it\nneeds nothing from the home folder.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":28,"oldLines":5,"newStart":28,"newLines":7,"lines":["   home), with an empty scratch HOME. Kimi's own install and sessions live in","   `~/.kimi-code`, which the profile opens."," ","-Codex logs in with an API key from the environment (`CODEX_API_KEY`), so it","-needs nothing from the home folder.","+Codex logs in from `~/.codex/auth.json` (`CODEX_API_KEY` and `OPENAI_API_KEY`","+are unset on the eval Mac). The unsandboxed `codex` lane reads it from the real","+home; `codex-sandboxed` copies it into the scratch `CODEX_HOME`, so its shell","+can read that copy."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false,"contentNotInModelContext":true},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01XHkirKbqUvtvwgnSs89HQi","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
