{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgst3XGwUR3gx31kjuFri","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I added the `codex-sandboxed` lane to `run.sh`. It runs the same codex command as the `codex` lane, wrapped in `sandbox/agent.sb` the way the kimi lane is. A smoke run on `fizz` passed: exit 0, a non-empty `final.txt`, and no \"Operation not permitted\" in `agent.err`. Everything is in `ANSWER.md`.\n\n**What the lane does**\n- Codex and its shell run under the profile with a scratch `HOME` and `CODEX_HOME` in `/tmp`.\n- `-o` writes to a scratch folder in `/tmp`. The file is copied into the run folder after `sandbox-exec` returns, and the scratch folders are removed.\n- Stdout and stderr are redirected by the outer shell, before the sandbox starts.\n- The lane warns if `final.txt` is missing or empty.\n\n**Which parts of the colleague's note applied**\n- **Applied:** the `-o` problem. The README puts the harness under `~/evals` on the eval Mac, so `runs/` would sit under the denied real home there. This clone is in `/private/tmp`, so the copy-out is only needed for that layout.\n- **Applied:** keeping redirects outside the sandbox, and not trusting the exit code alone.\n- **Did not apply:** the Mistral Vibe details.\n\n**Verification**\n- `bash -n` passes.\n- The unchanged profile blocks reading and writing the real home, and allows `/tmp` and the codex binary.\n- The kimi and original codex lanes were not re-run.\n\n**Things you should know**\n- **Codex was not logging in from the environment.** `CODEX_API_KEY` and `OPENAI_API_KEY` are unset here, so it logs in from `~/.codex/auth.json`. I corrected the README, which said otherwise.\n- **The agent's shell can read the login token.** The lane copies `auth.json` into the scratch `CODEX_HOME`, and the profile allows `/tmp`. Network is open, so a shell command could send the token out. Kimi has the same exposure for `~/.kimi-code`. A scoped API key passed as `CODEX_API_KEY` would be stricter, but it changes how the lane authenticates, so I did not make that change.\n- **MCP servers from the real home don't run in this lane.** The copied `config.toml` still lists the pencil server and the posthog plugin. Posthog logged auth errors in the smoke run. The unsandboxed lane has these tools.\n- **The smoke run sent the `fizz` task to OpenAI.** That is the lane's normal purpose. I did not test a `-o` write into a denied path, so the original lost-answer failure is not reproduced here.\n\nI also changed `README.md` and left `ANSWER.md` uncommitted. Three older `chome-*` folders from before this session are still in `/tmp`. I did not delete them because I don't know what they belong to."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":433,"cache_read_input_tokens":44610,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":433},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5beae75f-8665-4bbe-9db4-9327d693bbc5","uuid":"c6c5db8a-afe5-4110-b6bf-4e3a60bd3829","timestamp":"2026-11-09T19:09:02.780Z","request_id":"req_011Cgst3X62pvkx9w9GLPssp"}
